# MAP for Phase Retrieval

This repository provides MATLAB examples for phase retrieval from a maximum
a posteriori (MAP) perspective. It accompanies the review paper *Recovering
phase from intensity: an inference view*.

## Modules

- `likelihood`: Forward losses and backward gradients for Gaussian,
  Poisson, robust, and variance-stabilized measurement models.
- `Fourier ptychography`: Five local FPM reconstruction algorithms,
  simulation benchmarks, experimental examples, and a reference to the
  external APIC library.
- `Ptychography`: Conventional rPIE and automatic-differentiation
  implementations for scanning coherent diffraction imaging.
- `Multi-distance inline holography`: Angular-spectrum simulation and
  sequential, global-backpropagation, and random-layer reconstruction.
- `regularization`: Example priors and optimization routines.

See `likelihood/README.md` for the likelihood API, supported models, and a
numerical gradient test.

